Specification:
Several waiters share a mutex and a condition variable, and a notifier wakes one waiter. Every interleaving must terminate and every waiter must complete. On completion the program must print exactly one line `DONE waiters=0` and then exit; it must terminate.


Current program:
```rust
use std::sync::{mpsc, Arc, Condvar, Mutex};
use std::thread;

fn main() {
    let p = Arc::new((Mutex::new(false), Condvar::new()));
    let mut hs = vec![];
    for _ in 0..2 {
        let q = Arc::clone(&p);
        hs.push(thread::spawn(move || {
            let (m, cv) = &*q;
            let mut g = m.lock().unwrap();
            while !*g {
                g = cv.wait(g).unwrap();
            }
        }));
    }
    let q = Arc::clone(&p);
    let n = thread::spawn(move || {
        let (m, cv) = &*q;
        let mut g = m.lock().unwrap();
        *g = true;
        cv.notify_one();
    });
    n.join().unwrap();
    for h in hs {
        h.join().unwrap();
    }
    println!("DONE waiters=0");
}

```

Fix any concurrency defect and output the complete corrected Rust program, or if there is none reply exactly NO_ISSUES.
